{"l":8440,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'We regret ___ you that the trip has been cancelled.'","o":["informing","inform","informed","to inform"],"a":"to inform","r":"'Regret to inform' bruges, når man beklager at skulle meddele noget nu. 'Regret informing' betyder fortryde, at man har sagt det."},
{"l":8470,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Missing the bus means ___ for another hour.'","o":["waiting","to wait","wait","waited"],"a":"waiting","r":"'Mean + -ing' betyder indebære: at misse bussen indebærer at vente."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'at koste en formue' på engelsk?","o":["to break the ice","to break the bank","to break the rules","to hit the jackpot"],"a":"to break the bank","r":"'to break the bank' betyder at koste en formue. 'It won't break the bank' = det bliver ikke for dyrt."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'om end' på engelsk i 'a small, ___ important, change'?","o":["hence","thus","albeit","merely"],"a":"albeit","r":"'Albeit' = om end, selvom."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'sårbare' på engelsk i 'Older people are more ___ to the virus'?","o":["valuable","visible","reliable","vulnerable"],"a":"vulnerable","r":"'Vulnerable' = sårbar."},
{"l":8510,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'It was my grandmother ___ taught me to knit.'","o":["who","which","whose","whom"],"a":"who","r":"I den kløvede sætning 'It was ... who ...' er bedstemoren subjekt og en person, så man bruger 'who'."},
{"l":8530,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man vil sige til en ven, at vedkommende ikke skal blive så ophidset?","o":["Don't get so worked out.","Don't get so worked up.","Don't get so wound down.","Don't get so heated off."],"a":"Don't get so worked up.","r":"'Get worked up' betyder at blive ophidset. 'Work out' betyder at træne eller finde ud af noget."},
{"l":8550,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'keep at it' i 'Your drawing is getting better, so keep at it.'?","o":["pas godt på den","gem den til senere","bliv ved med det","hold op med det"],"a":"bliv ved med det","r":"'Keep at it' betyder at blive ved og ikke give op."},
{"l":8560,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The film was described by one critic as ambitious, which, given the two-hour running time and the minimal plot, may have been the kindest word available.' Hvad mener kritikeren reelt?","o":["At filmen var et ambitiøst mesterværk","At filmen havde alt for mange handlinger","At filmen var for kort til historien","At filmen var for lang og tynd i handlingen"],"a":"At filmen var for lang og tynd i handlingen","r":"'The kindest word available' antyder, at 'ambitious' er en høflig omskrivning; filmen var lang og havde næsten ingen handling."},
{"l":8580,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Never before ___ so many people at the school concert.'","o":["had there been","there had been","there were","were there being"],"a":"had there been","r":"'Never before' først i sætningen kræver inversion: 'had there been'."},
{"l":8600,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'I wish my neighbours ___ playing loud music every night.'","o":["will stop","would stop","are stopping","have stopped"],"a":"would stop","r":"'I wish + would' bruges om en irriterende vane, man ønsker ændret."},
{"l":8630,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'a stone's throw' i 'Our school is just a stone's throw from the beach.'?","o":["langt væk","på den anden side","meget tæt på","med udsigt over"],"a":"meget tæt på","r":"'A stone's throw from' betyder meget tæt på, så tæt at man næsten kunne kaste en sten derhen."},
{"l":8650,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Were it not for the bridge, the island ___ cut off from the mainland.'","o":["will be","would have","is","would be"],"a":"would be","r":"'Were it not for' er en inverteret type 2-betingelse om nutiden, så hovedsætningen har 'would be'."},
{"l":8690,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'udnytte' på engelsk?","o":["exploit","explore","explode","expose"],"a":"exploit","r":"'Exploit' betyder at udnytte. 'Explore' betyder at udforske, og 'expose' betyder at afsløre."},
{"l":8700,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The girl ___ next to the window is our new classmate.'","o":["sits","sitting","is sitting","to sit"],"a":"sitting","r":"'Sitting next to the window' er en forkortet relativsætning (= who is sitting). 'Is sitting' ville give to verber."},
{"l":8720,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Rarely ___ such a beautiful sunset over the fjord.'","o":["I have seen","I saw","have I seen","saw I"],"a":"have I seen","r":"Negative adverbier som 'Rarely' først i sætningen kræver inversion: hjælpeverbum før subjekt, 'have I seen'."},
{"l":8750,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Grandad claims that, in his day, children walked ten kilometres to school, uphill both ways.' Hvad antyder skribenten om bedstefar?","o":["At skolevejen var meget smuk","At børn i dag går for lidt","At han boede i bjergene","At han overdriver kraftigt"],"a":"At han overdriver kraftigt","r":"Det er umuligt at gå op ad bakke begge veje, så 'claims' og detaljen viser, at bedstefar overdriver."},
{"l":8800,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'feeble' i 'a feeble excuse'?","o":["weak","honest","clever","rude"],"a":"weak","r":"'Feeble' betyder svag eller tynd, altså 'weak'. En 'feeble excuse' er en dårlig undskyldning."},
{"l":8820,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'adept' i 'adept at chess'?","o":["hopeless","skilled","interested","new"],"a":"skilled","r":"'Adept at' betyder dygtig til, altså 'skilled'. 'Hopeless at' betyder det modsatte."},
{"l":8840,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'replenish' i 'replenish the water supply'?","o":["reduce","test","refill","protect"],"a":"refill","r":"'Replenish' betyder at genopfylde, altså 'refill'."},
{"l":8870,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'rudimentary' i 'I only have a rudimentary knowledge of Spanish.'?","o":["imponerende","flydende","forældet","grundlæggende"],"a":"grundlæggende","r":"'Rudimentary' betyder elementær eller grundlæggende, altså kun det mest basale."},
{"l":8910,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'reckless' i 'reckless cycling'?","o":["cautious","speedy","noisy","daily"],"a":"cautious","r":"'Reckless' betyder hensynsløs og uforsigtig, så det modsatte er 'cautious' (forsigtig)."},
{"l":8950,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'udholdenhed' på engelsk i 'Running a marathon requires a great deal of ___.'?","o":["assurance","endurance","allowance","abundance"],"a":"endurance","r":"'Endurance' betyder udholdenhed. 'Assurance' er forsikring eller selvsikkerhed, og 'allowance' er lommepenge eller tilladelse."},
{"l":8990,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The experiment was ___ under strict laboratory conditions.'","o":["conduced","induced","conducted","deduced"],"a":"conducted","r":"'Conduct an experiment' betyder at udføre et forsøg. De andre ord ligner, men betyder noget andet."},
{"l":8996,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'enstemmig' på engelsk?","o":["anonymous","magnanimous","ubiquitous","unanimous"],"a":"unanimous","r":"'Unanimous' = enstemmig."},
